WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.500
The evidence record remains useful after commissioning.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:08.380
Equipment generations change, suppliers revise components, and operators adjust workload or cooling

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:08.900
conditions.

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.740
Preserve enough configuration and revision control to recognize when the accepted envelope

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.380
has changed.

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.600
Review the interfaces affected by a proposed change.

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.240
A new component may fit while changing current demand, heat rejection, alignment

8
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.360
or control behavior.

9
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.380
A fluid change can affect multiple wetted materials.

10
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.340
A revised handling arrangement can change which loaded-route evidence applies.

11
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.980
Shared interfaces create opportunities for reuse and replacement, but substitutions still need

12
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.900
a supported basis.

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.380
Scale the review to the consequence of the change and retain the

14
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.580
decision and restrictions.

15
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.800
This is how openness becomes a practical operational benefit: more qualified options

16
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.900
with traceable boundaries, rather than more combinations whose behavior is assumed.

17
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.660
The same method supports future rack architectures even when their dimensions, voltage

18
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.080
or equipment packaging differ from today's examples.

